  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Journal first, ledger second",
      "items": [
        "The local journal is written before the ledger, so a ledger outage never loses the resume state",
        "The read order is the mirror image: ledger first, journal second",
        "A ledger outage degrades durability to machine-local, never to lost"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One snapshot, two readers",
      "items": [
        "The same document is committed as a ledger envelope and read back as a snapshot",
        "The commit carries the ledger auth token, which is why that flow is marked as policy",
        "The content hash makes a tampered record detectable, and the prompt hash makes a mismatched snapshot rejectable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What the plan still leaks",
      "items": [
        "The journal rebuild path is never called, so a broker restart loses the queue",
        "The ledger client is a generic HTTP port rather than a real EdgeRecord adapter",
        "Phase 1 of the roadmap closes both"
      ]
    }
  ]
